  "flood_prone_notes": [
    {
      "text": "During the 17 August 2026 habagat rains, Pasig opened 18 evacuation centers in 10 barangays: Bagong Ilog, Dela Paz, Kapasigan, Pinagbuhatan, Maybunga, Rosario, Santolan, San Miguel, Sta. Lucia and Ugong. Manggahan and Sumilang had centers on standby.",
      "sources": [
        "https://newsinfo.inquirer.net/2286819/pasig-evacuates-3189-residents-amid-habagat-rains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On 22 July 2025, rains displaced residents in 15 barangays: Bagong Ilog, Caniogan, Dela Paz, Kapasigan, Pinagbuhatan, Malinao, Manggahan, Maybunga, San Joaquin, San Miguel, Santolan, Rosario, Sta. Lucia, Sta. Rosa and Ugong. These barangays repeatedly need evacuation; most lie along the Pasig and Marikina rivers or the Manggahan Floodway (location inferred, not stated in the source).",
      "sources": [
        "https://newsinfo.inquirer.net/2085311/over-3000-families-in-pasig-city-seek-temporary-shelter-amid-rains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The DILG-NCR iDRRM profile lists Pasig's hazards as earthquake, liquefaction, fire and flood.",
      "sources": [
        "https://idrrm.ncr.dilg.gov.ph/lgu-profile/22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pasig DRRMO rescue bases (from the DRRMO Citizen's Charter, about 2022): Fire and Rescue Base at Red TC, Caniogan; San Joaquin Base on Elisco Rd.; Fire and Rescue Boat at Bambang-Kalawaan Bridge; Panthom (sic) Base at Mega Market, Palatiw; Falcon Base at Bartville Subd., Dela Paz.",
      "sources": [
        "https://assets.pasigcity.gov.ph/storage/attachments/disaster_risk_reduction_and_management_office/633f8800db42116651079686335211cbe1911664426268CCh_DRRMO.docx.pdf"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Evacuation centers are the ones the city opened during specific rain events in July 2025 and August 2026, as reported by Inquirer; this is not an official master list. verify=true marks a center that appears in only one of the two events. Health centers (barangay health centers) were not found."
